        "title": "Credit quality, capital and liquidity answer different questions",
        "text": "A provision recognises expected credit losses through an accounting allowance or charge. A non-performing loan is a loan classified as troubled under the applicable rules. Regulatory capital helps absorb losses, whereas liquidity is the ability to meet payments as due. A large deposit base does not remove the need to monitor these separately."
